message: "If you use these certificates or verifiers, please cite this release."
title: "MathIS Sidon Frontier: R9, R16 and Exact Two-Sided Certificates"
authors:
  - family-names: "Williams"
    given-names: "Ariel M."
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23548458"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/FromAriel/mathis-sidon-frontier"
abstract: >-
  Exact rational R9, R16 and seven asymmetric two-sided Sidon smoothing
  certificates with standalone standard-library Python verifiers. The strongest
  included certificate proves sqrt(ab) < 0.942810721 using Akwei's ramp
  construction within the Hou-Zhao lineage. It improves the cited Wu/wustep q2
  coefficient but remains above Akwei's reported stronger certificate. No
  current record, novelty, optimality, exponent advance or solution of Erdos
  Problem 30 is claimed. Development and review used AI-assisted workflows.
keywords:
  - Sidon sets
  - additive combinatorics
  - exact rational certificate
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Mathematical Integrity System
license: MIT
